SUMMARY:Gevity — cardio consistency grid on how-it-works (mirrors app #124)
DESCRIPTION:Ported the app's new cardio consistency grid (app-gevity-fit PR #124\, issue #112) into the static design source of truth — the how-it-works calendar the Rails grid was ported from.\n\nDeliverables:\n- Dual-band day cells: strength fills the top half\, cardio the bottom\; single fill for one modality\, a 50/50 split when both happened.\n- Added warm-clay cardio tokens to style.css :root — --color-cardio (#C2703D\, Zone 2 qualifying) and --color-cardio-light (#E8BE9E\, light movement).\n- Added "Zone 2 cardio" + "light cardio" legend entries and a realistic cardio mix in the recent real/current band (seeded history + future projection stay strength-only).\n- Scoped the dual-band CSS to .calendar-dual so the homepage grid (index.html) stays single-band and unchanged.\n- Verified in-browser at 380px (no horizontal overflow) and at desktop width.\n- Commit 97c331e on main (how-it-works.html\, style.css) — pushed to origin in the following session.\n\nRaw window (America/New_York): ~16:05 start (repo exploration + design preceded the commit\; launch.json/preview setup at 16:29) to 16:35:58 (ff-merge to main) plus completion report ~16:37. Rounded to 16:00–16:45.
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
